- `pnpm --dir apps/web test`, `pnpm --dir apps/web typecheck`, `pnpm exec eslint apps/web e2e`
- e2e spec 46, if a server can run: `E2E=1 cargo run --release -p jackioh-server` in one shell, then `pnpm --dir apps/web build:e2e && pnpm --dir apps/web exec vite preview --port 5173 --strictPort` in another, then `cd e2e && pnpm exec cypress run --spec cypress/e2e/46-menus-fit-one-screen.cy.ts`. CI's `e2e smoke` runs 46 on the pull request regardless. If you could not run it, say so; do not claim it green.

## Done when

- [ ] Steps 1–8: each selector in `TABULAR` carries `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`, and no other line in those sheets changed.
- [ ] Step 9: `index.css` has the section, with `p` first and then the balance rule. It uses `text-wrap-style` only and names no `.cf` selector.
- [ ] Step 10: the README sentence is added.
- [ ] `src/typography.test.ts` passes, and so do the existing tests listed above.
- [ ] The web's unit tests, typecheck and eslint are green. So are the harness checks (rustfmt, catalog, patches, rulings, clippy, cargo tests, web tests). None of them is touched, but run them as listed.
- [ ] e2e spec 46 is run (or reported as left to CI's `e2e smoke`).
- [ ] The report for the PR body includes `Closes #2123`, `Part of #2036`, the decisions below, and one line under `## Player note`, e.g. "The turn clock, prices, wallets, bars, ranks and stats no longer shift as their digits change, and headings break into even lines."

## Risks

- **Card faces' fit.** `font-variant-numeric` and `text-wrap-style` both inherit. Putting either on an ancestor of a `CardFace` would change what `cards/fit.ts` measures. Every selector above is a leaf or a list with no card in it (checked: `.collection-list`, `.shop-row__info`, `.packs-held`, `.stats-table`, whose thumb is a cost badge and not a face). `CardFace.tsx` renders no `p` or `h1`–`h3`, and no `CardFace` sits inside one. Do not widen any selector to a container.
- **The shorthand trap.** `text-wrap: balance` also sets `text-wrap-mode: wrap`. That would override an inherited `white-space: nowrap`, such as `lobby.css`'s visually hidden `.tavern.play-screen.play-hub .play-hero .brand`, which holds an `h1` and a `p`. Use only `text-wrap-style`. The test fails on the shorthand.
- **Layout and e2e 46.** `balance` keeps the line count, and Chrome's `pretty` moves only the last lines' words. Tabular digits are about `0`-wide. Neither should make a menu taller, but 46 is the check.
- **Exact-text tests.** `game/Clock.test.tsx` matches `.clock-grace .clock-digits { flex-shrink: 0; }` and `.clock-grace-label {…}` verbatim; leave them alone. `cursors.test.ts` slices `index.css` between `@media (pointer: fine)` and `html {`. The new section goes well after both.
- **The board's pixel acceptance (BUILD M5-T1).** No rule here changes size or spacing. `index.css`'s "SCOPED ON PURPOSE" note covers the shell chrome section, and the new section sits above it.
- No determinism, replay or hidden-information surface is touched (CLAUDE.md rule 7). Nothing is a `cargo` input.

## Open questions

These are decisions the plan takes. A person may overturn any of them, and the builder records them in the PR:

1. **`packs/pack-object.css` is not changed.** The issue lists it, but the pack object draws only the pack's name and the "Swipe or tap" hint, never a digit. The pack counts live in `packs.css` and `shop.css`. Rejected: a `tabular-nums` with nothing to align.
2. **`text-wrap-style` instead of the `text-wrap` shorthand.** This gives the same balance and pretty wrapping without resetting `text-wrap-mode` (see Risks). Rejected: the shorthand, which `auth/tavern.css` and `routes/landing.css` use on elements that inherit no `nowrap`.
3. **Large standalone values stay proportional:** `.stats-summary-value` (stats.css) and `index.css`'s `.stat-value`, whose comment already chose proportional figures on purpose. Also left alone: the flying `+N` (`.bar-flight`), the pack slot's outcome line, the stats games sentences and the Collection's Jlore line. None of these changes in place or stands in a column. Rejected: tabular everywhere a digit appears.
4. **The test lives at `src/typography.test.ts`, not `src/fx/`,** because the harness's web run excludes `**/src/fx/**`. It copies `fx/css.test.ts`'s parser instead of exporting it from there, because tests here keep their own helpers. Rejected: a shared `src/test/css.ts`, which would rewrite `fx/css.test.ts` for no gain to this task.
